# Day 05 – Microsoft Entra ID Self-Service Password Reset (SSPR)

## Objective

Configure Self-Service Password Reset (SSPR) in Microsoft Entra ID and understand the licensing requirements for advanced password reset features.

---

## Lab Environment

- Microsoft Entra ID
- Administrator Account
- Test User
- Microsoft Entra ID Free Tenant

---

## Tasks Performed

- Navigated to Password Reset settings.
- Enabled Self-Service Password Reset for all users.
- Attempted to configure Authentication Methods.
- Attempted to configure Registration settings.
- Verified tenant licensing requirements.

---

## Lab Result

The initial SSPR configuration was accessible. However, when accessing advanced Password Reset Authentication Methods, Microsoft Entra ID returned a licensing error.

Error:

> You need a Microsoft Entra ID Premium (P1/P2) license to use this feature.

---

## Technical Analysis

This behavior is expected because the tenant is using Microsoft Entra ID Free.

Advanced Self-Service Password Reset features require a Microsoft Entra ID Premium P1 or P2 license.

This lab demonstrates the importance of verifying licensing requirements before deploying identity management features in production environments.

